glm-cuda: a prompt chunk takes 4,096 rows again (1.3.0 dropped it to 2,048)

The pre-1.3.0 stack carried this as patch 0094. Upstream 1.3.0 ships prefill_rows = 2048, which
halves the rows each EXL3 experts call amortises its trellis weight decode over. Measured on this
pair: 2,048 -> 1,233/1,265 tok/s (8K/32K prompts), the 121-patch build with 4,096 -> 1,584/1,719.

Exact, not a numerics change: a pair's sums do not depend on the chunk size, so the gate is
identical greedy replies, not an NLL comparison. index_ring and solo_rows follow it (2x), so the
chunk's device scratch roughly doubles; both ranks must run the same value, which one image gives.

diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig
@@ -15,9 +15,9 @@
 const mlp = @import("cuda_mlp.zig");
 const kda_block = @import("cuda_kda_block.zig");
 
 /// A prompt chunk's rows (decode.PREFILL_ROWS).
-pub const prefill_rows = 2048;
+pub const prefill_rows = 4096;
 /// A decode window's rows (Engine's max_rows).
 pub const window_rows = 32;
 /// Prompts one prompt pass takes together (cuda_prompts): a prompt buffer's logits rows, one a prompt.
 pub const prompt_heads = 16;
